`wexample/symfony-content` is a small Symfony bundle for the code blocks inside authored content: it ships a front asset, {{ path("assets/ts/code-block.ts") }}, that highlights `.code-block[data-lang]` elements and Markdown `<pre><code class="language-…">` blocks with Shiki. It targets Symfony 8.2+ projects already built on `wexample/symfony-helpers`, where documentation or editorial pages live as Markdown files in the repository rather than in a database.

It used to carry a `markdown_file()` Twig function of its own, which read a file and converted nothing, next to a markdown dependency no PHP file here referenced. Markdown now has one owner in the suite, `wexample/symfony-template`, whose `markdown_file()` both reads and renders — see its cookbook. This package is what is left once that moved out: the browser-side half.
